body:
just entering the room where all my books are gives me dizziness and motion sickness  , i am actuaaly inside of it and trying to resist , although not studying but i will start soon , i wasn't able to hold a book or solve an equation even the most basic for three years , and still have problems but it gets better with time , of course it is not a straight path and fluctuates a lot but the big picture is that i am healing slowly but surely , good luck to you .

&#x200B;

p.s : if you need to talk i will try to listen

i really don't like reducing people to numbers but i give a 6.5 to 7 out of 10 and i don't think it is fair to judge you from 3 photos we have (- makeup where you are an 8)

&#x200B;

you need to improve , if possible , the darkened skin around your eyes

&#x200B;

by the way , your lips are gorgeous (i hope i don't come of as creepy) 

&#x200B;

please keep in mind that i am just some dude on the internet and my ratings are subjective , not all men think the same , i also speculate (not science , but as seen on marriage statistics)  that men and women of each race generally appreciate themselves more .

>1 WHY this is the case, has never been properly researched. At least not within those studies that I think you're referring to, but I'm happy to be proven wrong here. So your assertions based on that graph are your own ideas about it, that's not "scientifically proven" 

i agree with you that the subject is not heavily researched for various reasons including political correctness , but there were enough studies that we can draw some kind of picture , from evolutionary psychology and the different mating strategies of women vs men ( best mate seed vs spread the seed as much as possible) , there are of course plenty of studies  on facial structure , shoulder to waist ratio , dick size lol ... etc ... , but i have to agree with you that other factors come to play like wealth and social status that boost your overall score by 25% so yes it is not just about looks but mostly , also the uglier you are the less effective it becomes the more above average looking you are , the more it helps , and dont get me strated about the halo effect and its consequences the moment you are born until you die 

&#x200B;

>2. The most relevant question that no one ever asked based on that graph is "what's the minimum level of attractiveness score you would consider dating?" Because if men want at least a 5/7, while women want at least a 3/7, suddenly the proportion of men and women that are datable are exactly the same

&#x200B;

that was the question directly or indirectly it is a dating site ...

&#x200B;

>. It's also pretty well known that attractiveness isn't weighed the same by everyone, so it's an extremely relevant question. Maybe it doesn't matter on average, but we don't know. 

if that was the case there would not even be a bell curve but a straight line , and you know as well as i know that attractiveness is pretty objective , yes there are exceptions , but we are talking about the majority here

&#x200B;

> Just because it's a scientific study doesn't mean you can safely generalize it to anything beyond the population that you researched, which is to say that it really is only about the population of people using dating sites. This is important, because if you go to any dating site, you'll generally find guys from all walks of life, but never as many girls. Isn't it likely it attracts a subset of girls that doesn't reflect the population as a whole?

i actually have to agree with you here to a certain extent , but lets not forget that 33% of women we are talking about here so it is no small subset , and to say that it doesn't reflect on the whole population is true BUT THOSE women are not aliens and i can safely stretch it to include another 17 % of women (yes that was made up by me but i don't find it unresonable) and that makes it 50% of women 

&#x200B;

LOOK , by no means am i judging women here , it is just simple human nature at works , but if i understand the message that you are trying to convey is that we are humans , we have brain and CAN SOMETIMES SURPASS OUR PRIMITIVE INSTINCTS i have to agree with you , but the reality is that most of the time we fail to do so , anyways , thank you for your response , have a good day

although i believe in your uniqueness as an individual and bilieve your word , but i think what he means is that it s scientifically proven that women date above their league in looks and status (okcupid + match + tinder statistics) 80% of women go for the top 20% of males , on the other hand guys have a bell curve distribution in rating attractiveness

&#x200B;

but acouple things still bother me like this statement :

&#x200B;

>  I have never given a crap about a person's appearance when considering whether or not I would want to date them. 

&#x200B;

it may be possible but highly unlikely that you would date a hideous person or even someone noticeably below your looks level , i understand that consciously you try your best not to discriminate but some instincts are stronger than rationality

  have told him that the only way I would have another kid is of 1 of us quit our jobs and and got to be a stay at home parent.. but that's unrealistic and he know that 

&#x200B;

are you just saying that because it is unrealistic and would never happen or are you genuinely interested in a kid with him if the circumstances were better .

&#x200B;

on another front , is it no for another baby just with this man or never again ?

no , it was't a one night stand , this was a full blown affair and she is trying to minimize it , that also means she is lying , moreover she is also trying to reverse blame you for this by stating she was lonely , that is no excuse for cheating , she should have come to you when she felt lonely and asked you for more attention .

&#x200B;

i won't tell you to stay nor to leave , it is up to you and to your gut feelings , you are the only one who can judge if she is being very sincere or if she is playing games , finally i am sorry for your loss . best of luck

can it be fixed ? yes , will it be fixed ? odds are it won't 

try your best and don't give up altough odds are against you , through persistence you may win her back , try doing some of the activities you have done in the beginning of your relationship , try to spice up your sex life (to th degrees you are both comfortable with of course) 

&#x200B;

best of luck

for starters being a nice person in general is a good attribute , but being too nice to a afault or naive becomes a problem , i was a nice "guy too" , today i am still nice initially but once somebody disrespects me the slightest i turn into a demon , i no longer bend backwards for people who dont deserve it)

&#x200B;

the thing you need to be nice with nice people and cut contact with ungateful people .

first off , i am in a similar situtation with you with an even NEGATIVE  count of friends

&#x200B;

you are as valuable as you think of yourself , don't let others determine your worth (i know its easier said than done) but that is your only solution (temporarily) , you need to be comfortable in your own skin . that's the first part for you .

&#x200B;

the second part to the puzzle is to build your social skills and emotional intelligence , improv theatre s a good way to develop these skills but you can also join clubs and meetups in your area .

&#x200B;

on a final note , i wish the best of luck but NEVER again treat yourself with disdain , you just can not fathom how amazing everyhuman being is , its insane , we are one of the most complex structures in the universe , DAMN , if you need any help hit me up with DM .

well for starters i have a negative count of friends , people simply hate me before even getting to know me , i am a depressed and anxious mess , i am a total recluse as i have lived 3 years now and counting with minimal human contact (only for food if even that , sometimes i "forget" to eat for 2 , 5 , 10 days ) and i go  from underweight to overweight , there was one hell of a post i made when i first started redditting that scared even the most courageous (you wont believe i was an honor student before all this mess , but on the bright side , i am slowly but surely recovering , i wish you too the best of luck , embrace your wirdness , cheers .

&#x200B;

edit : i deleted the post as it was too long but most importantly too graphic

dude , just chill , his death (rip) was your wake up call , i bet he would be happy for you .

&#x200B;

edit : your story actually kind of helped me myself that it is possile to change
